Thank you, however as far as I can tell theta parameterization does not affect the default parameters set during the lavaanify function. That is:

lavaanify(model1,ngroups = 2) == lavaanify(model1, ngroups = 2, parameterization = "theta")

So unfortunately this does not resolve the issue.

On Wednesday, April 22, 2015 at 5:47:49 AM UTC+1, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:
> >
